-- Q3075: Risk Management and Economics [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Futures lock in $80/barrel regardless of spot; options expire worthless at $72 spot, saving $250,000 total versus futures","Futures are always preferred because they have no upfront cost and provide complete symmetric protection","Both strategies produce identical results because futures and options are economically equivalent instruments","Options are always preferred because they cost less than futures in every possible price scenario"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 815, futures lock Redstone into $80/barrel ($4,000,000 total), overpaying by $400,000 versus the $72 spot. Options expire worthless, so Redstone buys at spot ($3,600,000) plus the $150,000 premium, totaling $3,750,000 and saving $250,000. Futures suit price certainty; options preserve upside.
Wrong (B): Futures do have zero upfront cost but eliminate both upside and downside, making them suboptimal when prices fall.
Wrong (C): Futures and options have fundamentally different risk-return profiles and are not economically equivalent.
Wrong (D): Options require a premium that makes them costlier than futures when prices rise above the strike.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3075;

