-- Q3102: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Excluded from the transaction price entirely until the rebate period ends","Recognized only when the exact rebate amount becomes known with certainty","Included in the transaction price subject to the significant reversal constraint","Recorded as a separate liability until the rebate is realized by the customer"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 606-10-32-11, variable consideration such as volume rebates must be estimated and included in the transaction price, but only to the extent that a significant reversal of cumulative revenue is not probable when uncertainty resolves. This balances timely recognition with reliability.
Wrong (A): Excluding variable consideration entirely would be overly conservative and inconsistent with ASC 606''s measurement principles.
Wrong (B): ASC 606 requires estimation, not waiting for certainty; the constraint permits inclusion of reliably estimable amounts.
Wrong (D): The rebate reduces the transaction price rather than creating a separate liability independent of revenue.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3102;

-- Q3106: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Controls the specified good or service before transfer to the customer","Never takes physical possession of the goods before customer delivery","Receives a fixed commission from the supplier for facilitating the sale","Has no inventory risk exposure at any point during the transaction"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 606-10-55-36, the principal controls the good or service before transfer to the customer. Control indicators include primary responsibility for fulfillment, inventory risk, and pricing discretion. MarketHub exhibits all three, confirming principal status and gross revenue reporting.
Wrong (B): Physical possession is one indicator of control, but an entity can be a principal without it; conversely, lacking possession suggests agent status.
Wrong (C): A fixed commission is characteristic of an agent arrangement, not a principal relationship.
Wrong (D): Having no inventory risk is an indicator of agent status, the opposite of what defines a principal.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3106;

-- Q3113: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Never estimate variable consideration and exclude it from the transaction price","Always use the most likely amount method to estimate variable consideration","Include variable consideration only to the extent a significant reversal is not probable","Recognize variable consideration only when cash is received from the customer"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 606-10-32-11, the variable consideration constraint requires including variable consideration in the transaction price only to the extent that a significant reversal of cumulative revenue is not probable when uncertainty resolves. This prevents premature recognition of uncertain bonuses or penalties.
Wrong (A): ASC 606 requires estimation of variable consideration, not blanket exclusion from the transaction price.
Wrong (B): The most likely amount is one estimation method, but it is not always required; the expected value method is an alternative.
Wrong (D): Cash-basis recognition contradicts ASC 606''s accrual-based framework for measuring transaction prices.$EXPL$
