  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 606-10-25-27, a performance obligation is satisfied over time if the customer simultaneously receives and consumes the benefits as the entity performs. Janitorial services are a classic example because the cleaning benefit is consumed immediately as work is performed.
Wrong (B): A fixed delivery date relates to point-in-time recognition, not over-time satisfaction criteria.
Wrong (C): Payment terms (installments vs. lump sum) do not determine whether revenue is recognized over time or at a point.
Wrong (D): A warranty relates to assurance-type or service-type obligations, not the criteria for over-time recognition.$EXPL$
