UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Dividends received from the investee as revenue in the income statement","Only the fair value changes of the investment balance each reporting period","The investee''s revenue on a proportional basis as the investor''s own revenue","Its share of investee net income as investment income, dividends reduce the investment"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 323-10-35, the equity method requires recognizing the investor''s proportionate share of the investee''s net income as investment income, increasing the investment account. Dividends received reduce the investment balance rather than being recorded as revenue, reflecting the investor''s economic interest in performance.
Wrong (A): Under the equity method, dividends reduce the investment account; recording them as revenue applies to the cost method.
Wrong (B): Fair value changes apply to fair-value-option investments, not the equity method which tracks the investee''s earnings.
Wrong (C): The equity method tracks the investor''s share of net income, not revenue, from the investee.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3175;

-- Q3177: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Credits the investment account and debits subsidiary equity to eliminate both balances","Debits the investment account by $5,000,000 to increase the consolidated asset total","Records additional goodwill of $5,000,000 as a separate intangible on consolidation","Records revenue of $5,000,000 representing the subsidiary''s contribution to earnings"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): The basic consolidation entry eliminates the parent''s investment account (credit) against the subsidiary''s equity accounts (debit). Since the parent owns 100% and the investment equals the subsidiary''s equity ($5,000,000), the entry balances exactly. Any difference would be allocated to fair value adjustments or goodwill.
Wrong (B): The investment account is credited (reduced), not debited; debiting would double-count the subsidiary''s assets.
Wrong (C): Goodwill arises only when the acquisition price exceeds fair value of net assets, not from the elimination entry itself.
Wrong (D): The consolidation elimination is a worksheet entry; no revenue is generated from combining parent and subsidiary accounts.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3177;
